  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Scannable
  displayName: Blue Fire Algae
  scientificName: Alga Ignis
  description: A single upright column of cold cerulean fire, tapering to a blade's
    edge at its crown. It does not flicker, does not waver, and appears wholly indifferent
    to the currents about it, rather like a particularly smug candle. The surrounding
    flora wisely maintains a respectful distance. I have logged it as algae, though
    I harbour private doubts.
  journalImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 844bc4a5442612748b9222f327010cf6, type: 3}
